TIP:  Covered my many, many performers, this one is based on the version by Emmylou Harris.  She ends the song with an instrumental but another verse is often sung, which is included afterwards which you can continue with the (Am).

TIP:  For the intro, pick the 5th string <a> and strum (Am), then the 6th string <e> and strum (Am).  Repeat.  (Notes may or may not transpose.)

TIP:  In the chorus (Bm5) is just another way to play (F) higher up the neck for a nice treble lilt.  You can also just play a regular (F) if you'd rather.
    

